From 1e24ca37c01e7dd93095f53a13e2734b9d045f54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:35:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test(goldens): toolpath-goldens, the goldens as insta
 snapshots beside path goldens

A dev crate that runs every goldens/<set>/input.jsonl through the adapters in
process (read -> ir -> derive -> project to every other agent -> round trips
-> same-format -> shed -> known defects) and pins each stage as an insta
snapshot under crates/toolpath-goldens/snapshots/<stage>@<set>[@<agent>].snap,
with the agent, adapter and input sha256 in the snapshot header.

No manifest, no producer or environment pins, no child process: the input
bytes and the snapshots are the whole contract. Copilot's projection is pinned
in canonical form (sorted keys, session id masked) because `p export copilot`
mints a session id per run. The three known-defect TSVs become
known_defects@<set>.snap; a diff there is FIXED or WORSE and must be read.
`qualifier review` over the crate's own records is a second test, skipped only
when no binary is found and TOOLPATH_GOLDENS_QUALIFIER is unset.

path-cli's `path goldens` and goldens/manifest.json are left in place; the two
coexist in this spike.
